## 5. `HackerNewsScraper`

**File:** `backend/src/services/HackerNewsScraper.js`

### Relational diagram

```
HackerNewsScraper
    │ fetcher (injectable)
    ▼
news.ycombinator.com ──HTML──► cheerio parse ──► Entry[30]
    ▲
    │ called by
handleEntriesQuery / handleManualScrape / handleScheduled (worker.js)
```

| Related object | Relationship |
|---|---|
| Worker handlers | Call `scrape()` as the data source for API and cron flows. |
| Entry objects | Output shape: `{ number, title, points, comments }`. |
| Global `fetch` | Default fetcher; tests inject a mock fetcher (DIP). |

### Description & characteristics

Fetches and parses Hacker News HTML. Limits output to **30** entries. Handles missing points (“0”) and missing comments (“discuss” / absent link → `0`).

### Variables

| Name | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `DEFAULT_URL` | `string` (const) | `https://news.ycombinator.com/`. |
| `MAX_ENTRIES` | `number` (const) | `30`. |
| `this.fetcher` | `function` | `(url) => Response` — injectable HTTP client. |

### Constructor

| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `fetcher` | `function` | `(url) => globalThis.fetch(url)` | HTTP transport for testability. |

### Methods

| Method | What it does |
|---|---|
| `scrape(url?)` | Fetches HTML then parses; returns `Entry[]` (max 30). |
| `fetchHtml(url)` | Calls `fetcher`; throws on non-OK response; returns text body. |
| `parse(html)` | Cheerio load; walks `tr.athing` rows; builds entries with ordinal `number`, title, parsed points/comments. |

Module helpers: `parsePoints(scoreText)`, `parseComments(linkTexts)`.

### Related objects list

- Worker `handleEntriesQuery`, `handleManualScrape`, `handleScheduled`
- Entry plain objects

