## 9. Worker module (`worker.js`) — handlers & helpers

**File:** `backend/src/worker.js`

### Relational diagram

```
Cloudflare runtime
   ├── fetch(request, env, ctx) ──► handleFetch ──► routes
   └── scheduled(event, env, ctx) ► handleScheduled

handleFetch
   ├── OPTIONS → CORS
   ├── API key check (extractApiKey / isAuthorized)
   ├── GET /            → service info
   ├── GET /api/entries → handleEntriesQuery ── scraper + strategy + saveUsageLog
   ├── GET /api/scrape  → handleManualScrape ── scraper + saveEntries + saveUsageLog
   └── * /api/config    → handleGetConfig / handleUpdateConfig

createServices(env)
   ├── HackerNewsScraper
   ├── WordCounter + 2 strategies
   ├── FirestoreRestRepository
   └── apiKey (env.API_KEY)
```

| Related object | Relationship |
|---|---|
| `HackerNewsScraper`, strategies, `FirestoreRestRepository` | Assembled in `createServices` and injected into handlers. |
| `wrangler.toml` `[vars]` | Supplies `API_KEY` (and optional Firebase env overrides). |
| Frontend `api.js` | HTTP client calling these routes with `x-api-key`. |

### Description & characteristics

Main Worker entry: single fetch router for all HTTP traffic plus cron handler. Enforces static API key on every non-OPTIONS request. Exports only handler-related symbols (extra named exports break workerd).

### Variables (module)

| Name | Description |
|---|---|
| `CORS_HEADERS` | Allows origin `*`, methods, headers `content-type, x-api-key, authorization`. |
| `NO_FILTER` | Special filter id (local const — **not exported**). |

### Functions / “methods”

| Function | What it does |
|---|---|
| `json(data, status)` | JSON response helper with CORS. |
| `buildSaveReason(type, freqLabel)` | Audit reason string for manual/scheduled saves. |
| `describeFrequency(cron)` | `'0 */N * * *'` → `'each N h'`. |
| `extractApiKey(request)` | Reads `x-api-key` or Bearer token. |
| `isAuthorized(request, apiKey)` | Constant-time-enough equality check; fails closed. |
| `createServices(env)` | DI container for one request/cron invocation. |
| `handleEntriesQuery(url, services)` | Auth already passed; scrape → strategy or `NO_FILTER` → audit → JSON. |
| `handleManualScrape(services)` | Scrape → `saveEntries` → audit `(manual)`. |
| `handleGetConfig` / `handleUpdateConfig` | Read/merge `system_config`. |
| `handleFetch(request, services)` | Router + auth gate + error → 500 JSON. |
| `handleScheduled(services)` | Respect `cron_enabled`; scrape → save → audit `(each N h)`. |
| `default.fetch / default.scheduled` | Cloudflare entrypoints. |

### Related objects list

- `HackerNewsScraper`
- `MoreThanFiveWordsStrategy`, `LessOrEqualFiveWordsStrategy`
- `WordCounter`
- `FirestoreRestRepository`
- `wrangler.toml`

